== reading
- The backend's flag is settlement's own rule (backend/app/schemas/matches.py:120-148, _at_or_after_kickoff(published_at, kickoff)): a prediction published at 22:10Z on a 16:45Z kickoff is after kickoff, so True is the correct answer. The unpublish dialog's extra paragraph is expert.publication.kickedOffUnpublish (frontend/src/i18n/messages/expert.en.ts:105), shown for a fixture past its kickoff.
- The three specs assert the 'upcoming fixture' case (published_after_kickoff false; the plain unpublish text), but the helper selects by the stored status, which the clone never advances: the isolated backend runs with the scheduler off and was last synced 2026-10-18.
- So the three tests pass only while the first 'scheduled' fixture of the current UTC date is still in the future. Their last full pass, FINAL run 8 (2759f592), started at 07:41:29Z on 2026-10-21, before that day's first kickoff (16:45Z). The two live-isolated runs recorded after it (guard-after-live-isolated-expert.log at 12:15Z and FOLLOWUP 4a at 16:19:35Z) ran only expert-composer and expert-publishing, which do not assert the kickoff flags; every other recorded pass of these specs on 2026-10-21 started before 07:42Z.
- R1-rerun reproduced all three at 22:15:51Z, so the cause is deterministic, not flaky.
